    "related_formalizations": [
      {
        "identifier": "https://github.com/google-deepmind/formal-conjectures/blob/a6bf2bb646fc1926130c24781a3b3cf23d0ef288/FormalConjectures/Arxiv/math.0608009/PoissonConjecture.lean",
        "note": "Supplies the statements `poisson_conjecture`, `poisson_conjecture.variants.dimension_two`, `poisson_conjecture.variants.dimension_three` and `poisson_conjecture.variants.dimension_ge_two`, and the three definitions they use (`MvPolynomial.poissonBracket` comes from FormalConjecturesForMathlib/Algebra/MvPolynomial/PoissonBracket.lean). Challenge.lean and Poisson2/Defs.lean copy the definitions verbatim, with their names, and Challenge.lean copies the statements; scripts/check-fc-match.py checks this against Formal Conjectures at that commit. Palomar does not accept escaped name components such as «math.0608009» in theorem names, so Challenge.lean states the four theorems in the namespace PoissonConjecture, with Formal Conjectures' leaf names (for example PoissonConjecture.poisson_conjecture.variants.dimension_two); Solution proves them under both these names and Formal Conjectures' own. The basic bracket lemmas in Poisson2/Bracket.lean are copied from the same file, with one deprecated lemma name replaced. An earlier version of this repository (commit d464ff4) depended on Formal Conjectures directly and was linked from Formal Conjectures PR #7657.",
        "relationship": "builds-on"
      }
